<title>IRAQ: PRESS DIGEST - Iraq - Oct 9.</title>
<headline>PRESS DIGEST - Iraq - Oct 9.</headline>
<dateline>BAGHDAD 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>These are some of the leading stories in the official Iraqi press on Wednesday. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy.</p>
<p>IRAQ</p>
<p>- Iraq urges Iran not to interfere in its affairs.</p>
<p>- Iraq's Deputy Premier Tareq Aziz says the U.S. wants to control Iraq not to buy its oil.</p>
<p>(The above stories were also carried by THAWRA and JUMHOURIYA)</p>
<p>THAWRA</p>
<p>- Editorial on Iraqi-Turkish relations.</p>
<p>- Expatriates' conference in Baghdad concludes on Wednesday.</p>
</text>
